> That will only get him to the first level of the branch.

This is only the case if the first level is the only one that has been
visited so far - if you've been to level two (or deeper) on the quest,
you can reach these places when calling the portal function from
somewhere below the level where the portal existed.

So, getting thrown out of the quest for good will only make the game
unwinnable if you've not yet gone below the start level and/or if your
role is wizard.

> I dunno about this gathering the other invocation items thing,
> though--it seems to me that the proper responese is to switch alignment,
> slay the quest leader and his minions,

This would still require getting your hands on the Eye - the portal
will no longer exist. And for some chaotic classes, i find it quite in
character to attack/slay their quest leader anyway, without switching
alignment (the rogue quest boss just _begs_ for a death ray, i find).

